# A Pi's Wi-Fi list. Copy to configs/<pi>.wifi.conf (git ignores it, and
# tpi-ctl.sh keeps it mode 600: it holds passwords), then:
#   scripts/tpi-ctl.sh <pi> wifi sync
# One network per line, name::password, most preferred first. Only the first ::
# splits, so a password may hold anything; spaces count, at the ends too. Among networks in
# range, the Pi joins the highest on the list; ethernet still wins when plugged
# in. An empty password is an open network. Networks tunnel-pi saved before that
# aren't here are removed on sync. scripts/tpi-ctl.sh <pi> all syncs it too.
#
# MomsHouse::hunter2hunter2
# MomsHouse-5G::hunter2hunter2
# CafeGuest::
